      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Moradol was used for analgesia in 154 patients with unstable angina pectoris and small- and large-focal myocardial infarction and noubain in 69 patients aged 46 to 83. Moradol was found to be an effective analgesic for patients with acute myocardial infarction, exerting a hyperdynamic effect on the circulation, which was easily eliminated if the drug was combined with droperidol or relanium. Noubain is also effective in myocardial infarction, but exerts no hyperdynamic effect on the circulation."},
